###  https://crc1625.mdi.ruhr-uni-bochum.de/VirtualHandover
crc:VirtualHandover rdf:type owl:Class ;
                    rdfs:subClassOf crc:ProcessInstance ,
                                    crc:UnidentifiableProcess ;
                    rdfs:comment "A handover to which all measurements of a sample that were uploaded to the RDMS before any actual handover was logged. It will always act as the first handover of the chain on every sample, and may be part of a handover group alone or with other handovers." ;
                    rdfs:label "Virtual handover" .


###  https://crc1625.mdi.ruhr-uni-bochum.de/VolumeComposition
crc:VolumeComposition rdf:type owl:Class ;
                      rdfs:subClassOf pmdco:ChemicalComposition .


###  https://crc1625.mdi.ruhr-uni-bochum.de/WorkflowModel
crc:WorkflowModel rdf:type owl:Class ;
                  rdfs:subClassOf crc:ProcessModel ;
                  rdfs:comment """A model of a data workflow.

An instance of this entity will contain as its substep the beginning pf a sequence of WorkflowModelStep entities, each with a SHACL shape to be applied and (optionally) template key-value pairs.

Important: You can find instructions on how to assign workflow model steps to data workflows in the documentation for the assignedEntity property or the Python validation API."""@en ;
                  rdfs:label "Workflow model"@en .


###  https://crc1625.mdi.ruhr-uni-bochum.de/WorkflowModelInstance
crc:WorkflowModelInstance rdf:type owl:Class ;
                          rdfs:subClassOf crc:WorkflowModel ;
                          rdfs:comment """An assignment of entities to the steps of a specific WorkflowModel

A WorkflowModelInstance is composed of one or more WorkflowModelStepAssignment instances that indicate the entities to which the steps are validated against, alongside instructions on how to fetch the next target node(s) of the data workflow.

Important: You can find instructions on how to assign workflow model steps to data workflows in the documentation for the assignedEntity property or the Python validation API.""" ;
                          rdfs:label "Workflow model instance" .


###  https://crc1625.mdi.ruhr-uni-bochum.de/WorkflowModelStep
crc:WorkflowModelStep rdf:type owl:Class ;
                      rdfs:subClassOf crc:WorkflowModel ;
                      rdfs:comment """A WorkflowModelStep entity contains a SHACL shape to be applied to a target node and (optionally) template key-value pairs.

The target nodes will correspond to entities in a data workflow, and are dynamically assigned by the validation process following the WorkflowModelStepAssignment entities related to this step from a WorkflowInstance.

Important: You can find instructions on how to assign workflow model steps to data workflows in the documentation for the assignedEntity property or the Python validation API.""" ;
                      rdfs:label "Workflow model step" .


###  https://crc1625.mdi.ruhr-uni-bochum.de/WorkflowModelStepAssignment
crc:WorkflowModelStepAssignment rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                rdfs:subClassOf crc:WorkflowModelInstance ;
                                rdfs:comment """A WorkflowModelStepAssignment instance indicates the entities to which a workflow model step is validated against, alongside a reference to the property with which the validation process will fetch the next target node(s) of the data workflow.

Important: You can find instructions on how to assign workflow model steps to data workflows in the documentation for the assignedEntity property or the Python validation API.""" ;
                                rdfs:label "Workflow model step assignment" .


###  https://crc1625.mdi.ruhr-uni-bochum.de/WorkflowModelStepTemplate
crc:WorkflowModelStepTemplate rdf:type owl:Class ;
                              rdfs:subClassOf crc:WorkflowModelStep ;
                              rdfs:comment """A key->value template with which a WorkflowModelStep will replace values in its assigned SHACL shape.

The key and values are arbitrary strings. The logic for storing/reading/processing these strings must be specified by e.g. extending the WorkflowModel dataclass in Python.""" .


###  https://crc1625.mdi.ruhr-uni-bochum.de/XPSProcess
crc:XPSProcess rdf:type owl:Class ;
               rdfs:subClassOf crc:CharacterizationActivity ,
                               crc:UnidentifiableProcess ,
                               pmdco:AnalysingProcess ;
               rdfs:comment "A process where XPS measurements have been performed. Used by Activity instances and Activity Models to denote the type of measurements they refer to." .


